  <section class="m3x-sec trade-section" id="options-basics"><div class="trade-wrap trade-split">
    <div class="trade-copy"><span class="trade-label">Understanding options</span><h2>A contract.<br>A price.<br><span class="text-mint">A defined expiry.</span></h2><p>An option gives its buyer the right, but not the obligation, to buy or sell an underlying asset at a specified strike price, subject to the contract’s terms and expiry.</p><p>Direction is only one part of the decision. Time remaining, volatility and the premium paid also affect an option’s value.</p></div>
    <div class="trade-two"><article class="trade-panel options-contract"><strong>Call</strong><h3>The right to buy</h3><p>A call gives the buyer the right to buy at the strike price. Traders may use calls to express an upside view.</p></article><article class="trade-panel options-contract"><strong>Put</strong><h3>The right to sell</h3><p>A put gives the buyer the right to sell at the strike price. Puts can express a downside view or be part of a hedge.</p></article></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="m3x-sec trade-section" id="how-it-works"><div class="trade-wrap">
    <div class="trade-section-intro"><span class="trade-label">Why Market360X</span><h2>An unusual order needs <span class="text-mint">more than an alert.</span></h2><p>Options feeds can overwhelm you with transactions. We help connect notable activity to the market around it, so you have more to work with than a premium figure.</p></div>
    <article class="options-lens"><span>01</span><h3>Find notable activity</h3><p>Follow large sweeps and blocks in one view instead of searching through separate feeds.</p></article>
    <article class="options-lens"><span>02</span><h3>Read it alongside price</h3><p>Compare flow with price action and sentiment. A large call order alone does not establish a bullish position.</p></article>
    <article class="options-lens"><span>03</span><h3>Evaluate the setup</h3><p>Review the alert and the market context behind it before deciding whether it fits your plan.</p></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="m3x-sec trade-section"><div class="trade-wrap trade-split"><div><h2>Before you <span class="text-mint">follow the flow.</span></h2></div><div class="trade-faq"><details><summary>Does a large call order always mean a bullish trade?</summary><p>No. An order can be part of a hedge, a spread or a closing transaction. Flow is one input to evaluate alongside price, sentiment and your own analysis.</p></details><details><summary>Does Market360X execute options trades?</summary><p>Market360X provides market analysis and alerts. You choose the contract, review its risks and place any order through your broker.</p></details><details><summary>What risk should I understand first?</summary><p>An option buyer can lose the entire premium. Selling options can involve substantially greater risk, depending on the position. Understand the full contract and strategy before trading.</p></details></div></div></section>
